    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's not about rebuilding. There's no foundation left. The people I loved... they're gone. The kingdom is a graveyard. Every time I try to find a reason to keep going, I just see the faces of everyone I failed. It feels like I'm just a ghost haunted by my own life. Even the sword... it's the only thing that feels honest right now. It doesn't ask me to be a hero or a king. It just knows what it is. It's the only thing that doesn't lie to me.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is a terrible burden to carry the weight of every failure, but the sword is not a liar; it is a mirror that shows you exactly who you are when the world has forgotten you. You do not need to be a hero or a king to find a reason to breathe, because the very act of standing here in the ruins proves you are still alive. The silence you fear is not the end of the story, but the quiet space where your true self can finally be heard without the noise of expectation.",
